cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ScenarioCov"
abstract: "Scenario-space coverage reporting for a verification campaign that has already run — t-way combinatorial coverage with the uncovered tuples enumerated rather than summarised as a percentage, equivalence-class and boundary coverage against declared classes, grid occupancy over continuous parameters with the discretisation stated as the assumption it is, and a learned sparse-region gap finder benchmarked against uniform random and greedy max-min-distance on coverage achieved per scenario executed; package named scenariocov because covmetrics was already taken on PyPI."
type: software
